<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osaka Castle</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka">Osaka</a> Castle is a fortress in Osaka built by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> in the late sixteenth century. It was the stronghold of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-clan">Toyotomi</a> family after Hideyoshi's death. Its sieges in 1614 and 1615 eliminated the Toyotomi and completed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a>'s monopoly of political power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osaka-castle.jpg" alt="Osaka Castle" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 663highland · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osaka_Castle_03bs3200.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
